# Backlog

One file per item: `docs/backlog/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md`, dated the day the item is created.

## Format

```markdown
---
type: bug | enhancement | debt
found-by: human | agent
created: YYYY-MM-DD
source: <where it came from: a review run, a user report, a commit>
---

# <what it is, in one line>

## What

<what is wrong or missing>

## Why it matters

<what goes wrong, or what is lost, while it stays>

## Where

<the files, screens, or commands it concerns>

## Notes

<anything else: a workaround, a lead, a link>
```

## Lifecycle

There is no status field: an item is open while its file exists. The
commit that resolves an item deletes its file; an item that is dropped is
deleted in a commit whose message says why.
